  "instructions": [
    "Heat 2 tablespoons of lardons-render in a large pot over medium heat.",
    "Add the sliced onion and cook until translucent, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Add the caraway seeds and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Add the sauerkraut, pork lardons, cooking wine, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Stir to combine, then add the flour to thicken the stew.",
    "Bring the stew to a simmer and cook for 20 minutes, stirring occasionally.",
    "Taste and adjust the seasoning as needed.",
    "Serve the stew hot, garnished with chopped fresh parsley if desired.",
    "Serve 4-6 portions and enjoy!",
    "Freeze any leftover stew for up to 3 months for future meals."
